  "body": "It's not clear it's a good idea to allow overriding the way cross-origin resources are decoded. In particular overriding it with UTF-16 seems harmful. Overriding with replacement might be harmful too if it's some kind of injection attack and the script or stylesheet serves a vital purpose. Perhaps this too should use https://encoding.spec.whatwg.org/#get-an-output-encoding?\r\n\r\n(I suspect outlawing it completely for cross-origin resources is not possible, though if anyone can gather data on that, that would be even better.)\r\n\r\nNoted by @hsivonen at https://twitter.com/hsivonen/status/904942851091554305.\r\n\r\ncc @inexorabletash @mikewest ",
